    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "small steps dont really matter when the foundation is already gone. it's like trying to fix a single brick in a house that's already underwater. i dont see the point in \"reviving passion\" for something that is fundamentally broken. it feels more like i'm just being forced to witness a funeral that never ends. is there actually any dignity in just standing there and letting the tide take everything?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
